    "reflection": "There are many things by which the world teaches us to measure our lives: knowledge, achievements, influence, possessions, appearance and success. Yet God points us toward something infinitely greater—knowing Him.\n\nGod does not merely invite you to know facts about Him. He invites you into relationship with Him.\n\nYou may carry many titles: daughter, sister, wife, mother, friend, professional, entrepreneur, leader or minister. Some titles may describe you now; others may never describe your particular journey. But none is more foundational than this: you are a woman invited to know God.\n\nJeremiah reminds us that our greatest reason for confidence is not what we possess or accomplish, but that we understand and know the Lord.\n\nAs you begin this devotional journey, resist the temptation to make spiritual growth another achievement to complete. Come instead with an open heart.\n\nAsk God to reveal His character through His Word. Learn His ways. Listen to Him. Walk with Him.\n\nThe greatest transformation over these 365 days will not simply be knowing more Scripture. It will be knowing the God of Scripture more deeply—and allowing that knowledge to transform how you live.",
