    "theme": "Worship",
    "movement": "Knowing God",
    "scriptureReference": "John 4:23–24",
    "book": "john",
    "chapter": 4,
    "reflection": "Jesus' conversation with the Samaritan woman moved beyond debates about the correct geographical location for worship.\n\nThe Father seeks worshippers who worship in spirit and truth.\n\nWorship is larger than music.\n\nSongs can express worship beautifully, but worship encompasses a life responding to God for who He truly is.\n\nTruth matters because we do not worship a God of our own imagination. We worship the God who has revealed Himself.\n\nAnd genuine worship reaches beyond external performance into the heart.\n\nYou can sing without worshipping.\n\nYou can also worship while working, serving, giving, obeying, praying or quietly thanking God.\n\nThe question becomes:\n\nDoes my life increasingly declare that God is worthy?\n\nWorship moves our attention away from making ourselves the centre and restores God to His rightful place.",
