    "scriptureReference": "Psalm 37:4–5",
    "book": "psalms",
    "chapter": 37,
    "reflection": "“Delight yourself also in Yahweh, and he will give you the desires of your heart.”\n\nThis verse is sometimes treated as though God promises to grant every desire if we perform enough devotion.\n\nThe psalm offers something richer.\n\nAs we delight in God, our desires themselves are shaped by relationship with Him.\n\nThe closer you walk with God, the more you begin to value what He values.\n\nPrayer changes from merely asking God to support your plans to genuinely desiring His purposes.\n\nDelighting in God means finding Him worthy not only because of what He gives, but because of who He is.\n\nBring Him your desires honestly. You don't need to pretend you have none.\n\nThen hold them with open hands.\n\nAsk Him not only to fulfil your desires but also to form them.",
