    "book": "psalms",
    "chapter": 42,
    "reflection": "“As the deer pants for the water brooks, so my soul pants after you, God.”\n\nThe psalmist doesn't describe mild spiritual interest.\n\nHe describes thirst.\n\nWe know what physical hunger feels like, but spiritual appetite can be easier to ignore. We can fill our schedules, minds and attention so completely that we barely notice how thirsty our souls have become.\n\nSometimes we respond to inner emptiness by consuming more—more entertainment, more scrolling, more achievement, more shopping, more activity.\n\nYet some thirst cannot be satisfied by more stimulation.\n\nIt is thirst for God.\n\nSpiritual hunger can be cultivated. The more deeply you encounter God through Scripture, prayer and worship, the more precious His presence becomes.\n\nAsk God to make you hungry for Him again.",
