    "reflection": "Psalm 91 begins with dwelling.\n\n“He who dwells in the secret place of the Most High will rest in the shadow of the Almighty.”\n\nTo dwell is different from occasionally visiting.\n\nGod's presence isn't meant to be something we acknowledge only during emergencies or scheduled devotional time. We are invited to live with ongoing awareness of Him.\n\nThis does not mean faithful Christians are guaranteed freedom from every hardship. Scripture itself records godly people experiencing suffering.\n\nThe deeper promise is that God remains our refuge.\n\nTo abide means continually returning our trust to Him.\n\nWhen fear rises—return.\n\nWhen success tempts you toward independence—return.\n\nWhen disappointment makes you withdraw—return.\n\nWhen life becomes busy—return.\n\nMake God's presence your home.",
