    "book": "psalms",
    "chapter": 103,
    "reflection": "“Don't forget all his benefits.”\n\nForgetting God's faithfulness can happen surprisingly quickly.\n\nA prayer is answered, and soon another problem occupies our attention.\n\nGod carries us through one season, but the next difficulty makes us wonder whether He will be faithful again.\n\nBiblical remembrance deliberately looks backward so that faith can move forward.\n\nRemember God's forgiveness.\n\nRemember His mercy.\n\nRemember how He sustained you.\n\nRemember people He used to encourage you.\n\nRemember lessons learned in difficult seasons.\n\nRemember above all what He has done through Christ.\n\nGratitude does not require pretending everything in life is good. It means refusing to let what is difficult erase what God has done.\n\nCreate habits of remembrance.\n\nWrite things down.\n\nTell your testimony.\n\nThank God specifically.\n\nA remembering heart becomes a grateful heart.",
