    "scriptureReference": "Philippians 3:7–10",
    "book": "philippians",
    "chapter": 3,
    "reflection": "Paul had achievements, credentials and religious status.\n\nYet after encountering Christ, he reassessed what mattered most.\n\nHis great desire became:\n\n“that I may know him.”\n\nThis brings our first movement full circle.\n\nDay 1 began with the invitation to know God. Day 31 ends with a man who had discovered that knowing Christ was worth rearranging everything else around.\n\nKnowing God is not merely accumulating information.\n\nIt changes what we value.\n\nIt changes how we define success.\n\nIt changes how we respond to suffering.\n\nIt changes how we use our resources.\n\nIt changes our relationships, ambitions, decisions and priorities.\n\nAnd after thirty-one days, we have only begun.\n\nYou will never exhaust the riches of knowing God.\n\nSo don't measure this journey merely by how many devotional days you complete.\n\nAsk a deeper question:\n\n“Am I becoming a woman who increasingly knows, loves and follows God?”\n\nThat is the journey.",
    "declaration": "Knowing Christ is my greatest treasure. I will not measure spiritual growth merely by information or completed devotionals. I desire to know Him, love Him, follow Him and allow that relationship to transform my entire life.",
    "prayer": "Lord Jesus, above every achievement, possession, title and ambition, I want to know You. Deepen my love for You as I continue this journey. Transform my priorities, character and desires until my life increasingly reflects the One I am learning to know. Amen.\n\nMovement 1 complete ✅\n\nWe now have the entire first movement written:\n\nDays 1–15 — Who God Is\nDays 16–24 — Knowing God Personally\nDays 25–31 — Living in His Presence\n\n31 of 365 full devotionals are now drafted.\n\nThere is also a useful quality-control point before we write Day 32 onward: Movement 1 now gives us enough material to judge the real reading experience—not just isolated samples. The reflections are intentionally around a short daily-study length, declarations are Scripture-grounded, prayers flow directly from each passage, and Bible routing metadata is present for every day.\n\nNext is Movement 2 — Days 32–59: Jesus, Our Saviour & Lord, beginning with “In the Beginning Was the Word.”"
