    "slug": "you-are-the-christ",
    "title": "You Are the Christ",
    "theme": "The identity of Jesus",
    "movement": "Jesus: Our Saviour & Lord",
    "scriptureReference": "Matthew 16:13–17",
    "book": "matthew",
    "chapter": 16,
    "reflection": "Jesus asked His disciples two questions.\n\nFirst:\n\n“Who do men say that I, the Son of Man, am?”\n\nThen He made it personal:\n\n“But who do you say that I am?”\n\nPeter answered:\n\n“You are the Christ, the Son of the living God.”\n\nPeople continue to have many opinions about Jesus.\n\nProphet.\n\nTeacher.\n\nHistorical figure.\n\nMoral example.\n\nRevolutionary.\n\nBut eventually every disciple must confront Jesus' question personally.\n\nWho do you say He is?\n\nCalling Jesus the Christ is more than agreeing with a theological statement. If He truly is God's promised Messiah and Lord, that truth demands a response.\n\nYou cannot meaningfully confess Jesus as Lord while insisting upon being the ultimate authority over your own life.\n\nFaith moves from information about Jesus to allegiance to Jesus.\n\nSo allow His question to reach beyond the page today.\n\nWho is Jesus to you?\n\nAnd does the way you live agree with your answer?",
    "declaration": "Jesus is the Christ, the Son of the living God. I confess Him as my Saviour and Lord, and I will increasingly bring every area of my life under His authority.",
    "prayer": "Father, reveal Christ to me more deeply. Jesus, I confess that You are the Christ, the Son of the living God. Expose any area where my life contradicts that confession and teach me to follow You wholeheartedly. Amen."
