    "reflection": "Jesus calls Himself the Good Shepherd.\n\nA shepherd leads, protects, knows and cares for the sheep.\n\nJesus contrasts Himself with hired workers who flee when danger comes. The Good Shepherd does not abandon His sheep.\n\nHe lays down His life for them.\n\nThat image gives us both comfort and direction.\n\nComfort, because you are not shepherding your own soul alone.\n\nDirection, because sheep are meant to follow the shepherd.\n\nWe often want Christ’s protection while resisting His leadership.\n\nBut His care and authority belong together.\n\nThe Shepherd who knows you also knows where He is leading.\n\nYou may not always understand the route, but you can trust His character.\n\nThe safest place for the sheep is not wherever the sheep prefers to wander.\n\nIt is near the Shepherd.",
