    "slug": "saved-by-grace",
    "title": "Saved by Grace",
    "theme": "Salvation by grace",
    "movement": "Jesus: Our Saviour & Lord",
    "scriptureReference": "Ephesians 2:8–10",
    "book": "ephesians",
    "chapter": 2,
    "reflection": "Paul makes the order clear:\n\nsaved by grace through faith → created for good works.\n\nGood works are the result of salvation, not the price of admission.\n\nThat distinction matters.\n\nIf our works saved us, we could boast.\n\nIf our failures permanently disqualified us from grace, none of us could stand.\n\nSalvation is God’s gift.\n\nYet grace does not leave us unchanged.\n\nThe same passage that says we are not saved by works says we are created in Christ Jesus for good works.\n\nGrace is neither legalism nor spiritual laziness.\n\nWe don't obey so God will finally love us.\n\nWe obey because in Christ we have received a salvation we could never earn.\n\nThat produces gratitude.\n\nAnd gratitude begins to produce a transformed life.",
