    "reflection": "Jesus promised His disciples another Helper who would remain with them.\n\nThe Spirit of truth would not merely work around them.\n\nJesus said:\n\n“He lives with you, and will be in you.”\n\nThe Holy Spirit is personal.\n\nHe teaches.\n\nGuides.\n\nSpeaks.\n\nHelps.\n\nIntercedes.\n\nGlorifies Christ.\n\nAnd because He is personal, our response to Him cannot be reduced to chasing spiritual sensations.\n\nKnowing the Holy Spirit means growing in awareness of God's presence, submitting to His work and learning to walk according to Scripture.\n\nIt also means remembering the Spirit's central purpose is not to make us fascinated with ourselves.\n\nJesus said the Spirit would glorify Him.\n\nA genuinely Spirit-centred life therefore becomes increasingly Christ-centred.\n\nThe more deeply the Spirit works in us, the more precious Jesus becomes.",
