    "book": "1-corinthians",
    "chapter": 6,
    "reflection": "Paul asks believers:\n\n“Don't you know that your body is a temple of the Holy Spirit who is in you?”\n\nThat truth gives extraordinary dignity to ordinary Christian life.\n\nGod's presence is not restricted to a church building.\n\nFor the believer, the Holy Spirit dwells within.\n\nPaul uses this truth specifically to address how Christians use their bodies.\n\nOur bodies therefore matter spiritually.\n\nWhat we do sexually matters.\n\nHow we treat ourselves matters.\n\nWhat we allow to master us matters.\n\nOur physical lives cannot be separated from discipleship.\n\nThe body is not something worthless that the “spiritual” part of us must escape.\n\nIt belongs to God.\n\nThis also means your ordinary Monday can be lived in awareness of God's presence just as genuinely as Sunday worship.\n\nYou carry your relationship with God into the office, kitchen, classroom, marketplace and home.",
    "declaration": "My body belongs to God and is a temple of the Holy Spirit. I will honour God not only with my thoughts and words but with the way I live physically.",
