    "reflection": "One of the deepest human desires is to belong.\n\nWe search for belonging in relationships, communities, careers, families, social groups and approval.\n\nThese relationships can be valuable, but none can carry the full weight of our identity.\n\nPaul gives believers a deeper belonging:\n\nyou belong to Christ.\n\nThe presence of the Spirit marks a new identity and allegiance.\n\nThis matters particularly when following Jesus makes you feel different from people around you.\n\nThere may be convictions you cannot abandon simply to fit in.\n\nChoices others do not understand.\n\nRelationships where approval is conditional upon becoming someone God has not called you to be.\n\nBelonging to Christ gives us freedom from making human acceptance ultimate.\n\nYou can love people deeply without asking them to define your worth.\n\nYou already belong.",
