    "reflection": "The Spirit does more than assure believers that they belong to Christ.\n\nPaul says we have received the Spirit of adoption.\n\nThrough Him we cry:\n\n“Abba! Father!”\n\nChristian salvation is not merely the cancellation of a debt.\n\nIt brings us into God's family.\n\nThis does not mean every believer's relationship with God will always feel emotionally close. Feelings fluctuate.\n\nAdoption is a reality grounded in God's saving action.\n\nYou do not have to approach God as a terrified outsider trying to persuade Him to let you stay.\n\nIn Christ, you come as His child.\n\nAnd the Spirit bears witness to that relationship.\n\nFor women whose experiences of family have included rejection, instability or disappointment, this truth can take time to settle deeply into the heart.\n\nLet Scripture redefine family at its highest level.\n\nYou have a Father.\n\nYou belong in His household.",
