    "reflection": "Paul tells believers that after hearing and believing the gospel, they were sealed with the promised Holy Spirit.\n\nIn the ancient world, a seal could communicate ownership, authenticity and security.\n\nPaul then describes the Spirit as the guarantee of our inheritance.\n\nOur assurance is therefore not built upon maintaining a constant spiritual feeling.\n\nSome days you may feel deeply aware of God.\n\nOther days your emotions may be flat.\n\nThe gospel remains true.\n\nGod's promises do not become less reliable because your feelings fluctuate.\n\nThe Spirit points us toward the certainty of what God has promised to complete.\n\nThis does not encourage complacency. Genuine assurance should produce gratitude, worship and holy living.\n\nBut it does free us from constantly asking whether one difficult day means God has abandoned us.\n\nGod finishes what He begins.",
