    "scriptureReference": "Romans 8:15–16",
    "book": "romans",
    "chapter": 8,
    "reflection": "“The Spirit himself testifies with our spirit that we are children of God.”\n\nFear asks:\n\nDo I really belong?\n\nThe gospel answers by pointing us away from our performance and toward God's saving work.\n\nPaul contrasts slavery producing fear with adoption producing relationship.\n\nThe Spirit does not lead believers into a life of constant terror that one imperfect moment has removed them from God's family.\n\nAt the same time, assurance is not permission to disregard holiness.\n\nThe same Romans 8 that speaks about adoption also speaks about putting sinful practices to death.\n\nSecure children still learn obedience.\n\nBut obedience flows from belonging rather than attempting to purchase belonging.\n\nThere is a tremendous difference between:\n\n“I must make God accept me.”\n\nand:\n\n“Because I belong to God, I want to live as His daughter.”\n\nLet the second shape your discipleship.",
