    "scriptureReference": "John 14:16–18",
    "book": "john",
    "chapter": 14,
    "reflection": "Jesus knew His disciples were about to face a painful transition.\n\nHe was leaving.\n\nYet He promised:\n\n“I will not leave you orphans.”\n\nHe promised another Helper who would remain with them.\n\nThere are seasons when loneliness is not solved simply by having more people around us.\n\nYou can be surrounded and still feel alone.\n\nYou can carry responsibilities nobody fully understands.\n\nYou can walk through transitions where familiar support changes.\n\nJesus does not promise believers constant human companionship.\n\nHe promises something deeper:\n\nGod's presence.\n\nThe Holy Spirit is not a substitute for healthy Christian community—we need one another.\n\nBut even the best human relationship cannot be present every moment.\n\nGod can.\n\nWhen loneliness whispers, “Nobody is here,” remember the promise of Christ.\n\nYou have not been abandoned.",
