    "chapter": 8,
    "reflection": "“For as many as are led by the Spirit of God, these are children of God.”\n\nBeing Spirit-led is sometimes discussed almost entirely in terms of major decisions:\n\nWhich job?\n\nWhich city?\n\nWhich opportunity?\n\nBut Romans 8 places the Spirit's leadership within a much larger context: living as God's children and putting sinful ways to death.\n\nThe Spirit leads us toward holiness.\n\nToward truth.\n\nToward Christlikeness.\n\nSo before asking for extraordinary guidance, pay attention to ordinary obedience.\n\nIf Scripture has already told us to forgive, tell the truth, flee sexual immorality, love our neighbour or act justly, we do not need a special revelation to decide whether obedience applies.\n\nLearning the Spirit's leadership begins with becoming responsive to what God has already made clear.",
