    "reflection": "Paul does not tell believers merely to suppress every sinful desire through determination.\n\nHe says:\n\n“Walk by the Spirit.”\n\nThe Christian life involves a real conflict.\n\nOld desires do not always disappear immediately because we belong to Christ. There remains a battle between the flesh and the Spirit.\n\nThat battle does not mean your faith is fake.\n\nIt means you need daily dependence.\n\nWalking describes continual movement.\n\nOne decision.\n\nThen another.\n\nOne response.\n\nOne conversation.\n\nOne temptation.\n\nOne act of obedience at a time.\n\nVictory is often less dramatic than we imagine.\n\nIt may look like closing the browser.\n\nRefusing the gossip.\n\nControlling the angry response.\n\nChoosing honesty.\n\nLeaving the unhealthy situation.\n\nAsking forgiveness.\n\nWalking away from what repeatedly draws you into sin.\n\nAnd in each moment:\n\n“Holy Spirit, help me choose what honours Christ.”",
