    "reflection": "“If we live by the Spirit, let's also walk by the Spirit.”\n\nAnother translation expresses the idea as keeping in step with the Spirit.\n\nIt is an image of alignment.\n\nWe can be eager for God to bless the direction we have already chosen while resisting His correction when He leads differently.\n\nKeeping in step requires attentiveness.\n\nPerhaps the Spirit uses Scripture to confront your attitude.\n\nPerhaps conviction comes during a conversation.\n\nPerhaps you recognise that your pace has become unhealthy.\n\nPerhaps you need to apologise instead of defending yourself.\n\nThe question becomes:\n\nWill I adjust my steps?\n\nWalking with the Spirit is not merely about dramatic moments.\n\nIt is responsive discipleship.\n\nAnd small acts of responsiveness, repeated over time, shape character.",
