    "reflection": "Paul tells believers:\n\n“Don't grieve the Holy Spirit of God.”\n\nThe surrounding verses are strikingly practical.\n\nCorrupt speech.\n\nBitterness.\n\nWrath.\n\nAnger.\n\nMalice.\n\nThen kindness, tenderheartedness and forgiveness.\n\nSometimes we search for highly mysterious explanations for spiritual dryness while ignoring very ordinary disobedience.\n\nHow we speak to people matters to God.\n\nHow long we nurse resentment matters.\n\nHow we treat people who disappoint us matters.\n\nBecause the Holy Spirit is personal, sin is not merely breaking an abstract rule.\n\nIt grieves the God who dwells within His people.\n\nThe appropriate response is not shame-driven hiding.\n\nIt is repentance.\n\nAsk:\n\nIs there something in my conduct that I know does not please God?\n\nThen deal with it honestly.",
