    "reflection": "Paul gives two instructions that belong together:\n\n“Don't quench the Spirit.”\n\nand\n\n“Test all things. Hold firmly that which is good.”\n\nThis is wonderfully balanced.\n\nWe are not called to cynical unbelief that dismisses everything spiritual.\n\nNeither are we called to gullibility that accepts every claim made in God's name.\n\nWe need openness and discernment.\n\nDo not quench.\n\nDo test.\n\nDo hold onto what is good.\n\nReject what is evil.\n\nA mature Spirit-filled church—and a mature Spirit-filled woman—does not fear biblical examination.\n\nTruth can withstand testing.\n\nWhen someone says, “God told me,” we are not required to switch off discernment.\n\nWe test teaching and spiritual claims according to Scripture.\n\nThe Holy Spirit does not need us to protect falsehood in order to honour Him.",
