    "reflection": "Jesus said the Holy Spirit would convict the world concerning sin, righteousness and judgment.\n\nConviction is a gift.\n\nWithout it, we could become comfortable with what is destroying us.\n\nBut conviction and condemnation are not the same.\n\nCondemnation says:\n\n“Hide from God. There is no hope for you.”\n\nGodly conviction says:\n\n“This is sin. Bring it into the light. Turn back to God.”\n\nThe Holy Spirit does not expose sin because He delights in humiliation.\n\nHe leads us toward truth and repentance.\n\nWhen conviction comes, resist two opposite responses.\n\nDon't excuse the sin.\n\nAnd don't collapse into hopeless shame.\n\nAgree with God.\n\nConfess.\n\nReceive the grace available in Christ.\n\nMake whatever practical changes repentance requires.\n\nThen continue walking.",
