    "reflection": "After describing the armour of God, Paul tells believers to pray “at all times in the Spirit.”\n\nPrayer is part of spiritual warfare.\n\nBut praying in the Spirit is not a technique for manipulating outcomes.\n\nIt is prayer under the Spirit's influence—aligned with God's truth, dependent upon His strength and persistent in intercession.\n\nNotice Paul's words:\n\nat all times.\n\nwith all prayer.\n\nwith perseverance.\n\nSpirit-led prayer produces persistence, not merely intensity.\n\nSome prayers require continuing long after the initial emotion has faded.\n\nKeep praying for the person.\n\nKeep praying for wisdom.\n\nKeep praying for the Church.\n\nKeep praying for God's Kingdom purposes.\n\nBut as you persist, keep surrendering the outcome to God.\n\nPersistent prayer is not forcing God's hand.\n\nIt is continuing to entrust the matter into it.",
