    "reflection": "Pentecost marks an extraordinary moment in God's redemptive story.\n\nThe promised Spirit was poured out.\n\nThe disciples spoke as the Spirit enabled them.\n\nPeter proclaimed Christ.\n\nPeople were convicted.\n\nThousands responded to the gospel.\n\nAnd a new community emerged devoted to teaching, fellowship, breaking bread and prayer.\n\nPentecost is more than a dramatic spiritual event.\n\nIt propels the Church into mission.\n\nThe Spirit creates a people centred upon Jesus and empowered to carry the gospel across cultural and geographical boundaries.\n\nThis matters for our understanding of Christian community.\n\nWe are not saved merely into private spirituality.\n\nWe become part of Christ's people.\n\nWe need Scripture.\n\nFellowship.\n\nPrayer.\n\nWorship.\n\nService.\n\nMission.\n\nThe Spirit who dwells within individual believers also forms us into a body.\n\nYou were never intended to follow Jesus entirely alone.",
