    "book": "romans",
    "chapter": 12,
    "reflection": "After eleven chapters explaining God's mercy, Paul calls believers to respond:\n\n“Present your bodies a living sacrifice, holy, acceptable to God.”\n\nThis is where our first thirty-one days on the Holy Spirit should lead:\n\nsurrender.\n\nWe can learn terminology about the Spirit.\n\nStudy spiritual gifts.\n\nDiscuss guidance.\n\nDesire power.\n\nSeek experiences.\n\nBut if we continually resist God's authority, we have missed the point.\n\nThe Spirit works to transform us into people whose lives increasingly belong to God.\n\nSurrender is not a one-time emotional moment.\n\nTomorrow there will be another decision.\n\nAnother thought to bring under Christ.\n\nAnother opportunity to obey.\n\nAnother desire to surrender.\n\nAnother place to trust.\n\nThe Spirit-filled life is the yielded life.\n\nNot perfection.\n\nNot passivity.\n\nBut a continuing:\n\n“Yes, Lord. My life is Yours.”",
