    "reflection": "Hebrews describes faith as confidence in what we hope for and assurance about what we do not see.\n\nBiblical faith is not wishful thinking.\n\nIt is not pretending uncertainty does not exist.\n\nIt is not forcing yourself to feel positive.\n\nFaith rests upon the character and promises of God.\n\nThat means the strength of your faith is not measured simply by how certain you feel emotionally. There are days when trust may be accompanied by trembling.\n\nFaith can say:\n\n“I do not see the whole picture, but I know who God is.”\n\nHebrews 11 is filled with people who acted because they trusted God before seeing the outcome.\n\nFaith therefore has movement in it.\n\nIt listens.\n\nBelieves.\n\nObeys.\n\nWaits.\n\nEndures.\n\nThe question is not merely whether you believe God exists.\n\nIt is whether you are learning to entrust your life to Him.",
