    "reflection": "Paul tells us:\n\n“Faith comes by hearing, and hearing by the word of Christ.”\n\nFaith grows where truth is heard and received.\n\nIf your mind is constantly filled with fear, comparison, outrage, pressure and self-doubt, those voices will shape the way you see God and your circumstances.\n\nScripture interrupts those voices with truth.\n\nIt reminds you who God is.\n\nWhat Christ has done.\n\nWhat God has promised.\n\nWhat obedience looks like.\n\nFaith is not strengthened merely by repeating encouraging phrases to yourself. It is strengthened by exposure to God's Word.\n\nThis is why Scripture needs to become more than emergency medicine.\n\nIt should become daily nourishment.\n\nThe more deeply God's Word settles into you, the more truth becomes available when circumstances challenge your trust.\n\nFeed your faith deliberately.",
    "declaration": "I will strengthen my faith by listening to God's Word. I choose to give Scripture greater authority than the fearful or distracting voices around me.",
    "prayer": "Lord, deepen my hunger for Your Word. Help me recognise what is shaping my thinking and let Scripture become the strongest voice in my life. Amen."
