    "reflection": "“Let us hold fast the confession of our hope without wavering; for he who promised is faithful.”\n\nThe verse does not tell us to hold on because we are strong.\n\nIt tells us to hold on because He is faithful.\n\nThat distinction changes everything.\n\nIf hope depended upon our emotional consistency, it would be fragile.\n\nSome days you feel confident.\n\nOther days you feel weary.\n\nGod's faithfulness does not fluctuate with your mood.\n\nWhen Scripture calls us to perseverance, the foundation is always God's character.\n\nThis does not mean every personal expectation is a promise from God.\n\nWe must distinguish what God has actually promised from what we simply hope He will do.\n\nBut where God has spoken clearly, His character is trustworthy.\n\nHold onto Him.",
