    "book": "luke",
    "chapter": 1,
    "reflection": "The angel's words to Mary were:\n\n“For nothing spoken by God is impossible.”\n\nThe context matters.\n\nThis was not a generic promise that every dream a person imagines will happen.\n\nIt was assurance that what God had spoken concerning His redemptive purpose would not fail.\n\nThat gives us a healthier foundation for confidence.\n\nGod is able to accomplish what He purposes.\n\nHis power is not limited by the circumstances that limit us.\n\nBut faith in God's power must remain joined to surrender to God's will.\n\nWe can ask boldly.\n\nDream faithfully.\n\nAttempt difficult things in obedience.\n\nBut we do not turn God's omnipotence into a guarantee that He must fulfil every personal desire.\n\nOur confidence is:\n\nGod can do what He chooses, and His purposes cannot be defeated.",
