    "chapter": 9,
    "reflection": "The father's prayer is one of the most honest in Scripture:\n\n“I believe. Help my unbelief!”\n\nFaith and struggle can exist in the same heart.\n\nSometimes we think real faith means never experiencing doubt, questions or fear.\n\nThis father shows us another path.\n\nHe brought his imperfect faith directly to Jesus.\n\nHe did not pretend.\n\nHe did not wait until his confidence felt complete.\n\nHe asked Jesus to help the part of him that still struggled.\n\nYou can do the same.\n\nGod is not threatened by honest questions.\n\nBring them into His presence.\n\nSearch Scripture.\n\nSeek wise counsel.\n\nPray.\n\nDon't romanticise doubt, but don't hide it either.\n\nFaith grows when uncertainty drives us toward Christ rather than away from Him.",
