    "reflection": "We have already seen Jesus calm the storm.\n\nNow consider the disciples' faith.\n\nTheir fear was understandable.\n\nThe boat was filling.\n\nBut Jesus asked:\n\n“Why are you so afraid? How is it that you have no faith?”\n\nThe issue was not whether the storm existed.\n\nThe issue was what they believed about Jesus in the middle of it.\n\nStorms expose our theology.\n\nIt is easy to say God is trustworthy when life is predictable.\n\nTrouble reveals what we actually believe.\n\nDoes difficulty mean God no longer cares?\n\nDoes delay mean He is absent?\n\nDoes fear mean faith has vanished?\n\nNot necessarily.\n\nFaith does not mean you never feel afraid.\n\nIt means fear does not become your lord.",
