    "reflection": "God's answer to fear is repeatedly connected to His presence:\n\n“Don't be afraid, for I am with you.”\n\nNotice what He does not say:\n\nNothing difficult will ever happen.\n\nThe deeper promise is:\n\nI am with you.\n\nFear often imagines a future where we must face everything alone.\n\nGod inserts Himself into that imagined future.\n\nWhatever comes, He will still be God.\n\nFaith does not require us to become naturally fearless personalities.\n\nCourage is often obedience while fear is still talking.\n\nTake the appointment.\n\nHave the necessary conversation.\n\nApply.\n\nBegin.\n\nWait.\n\nSpeak.\n\nStay.\n\nLeave—when wisdom and obedience require it.\n\nAnd remember:\n\nyou do not enter tomorrow before God gets there.",
