    "chapter": 14,
    "reflection": "Peter stepped out of the boat because Jesus said:\n\n“Come.”\n\nThat matters.\n\nFaith is not reckless action we invent and then expect God to support.\n\nPeter's courage was a response to Christ's word.\n\nHe stepped out.\n\nThen he became distracted by the wind and began to sink.\n\nJesus reached for him.\n\nThere is both challenge and comfort here.\n\nChallenge: sometimes obedience requires leaving what feels safe.\n\nComfort: failure in the middle of obedience does not mean Jesus disappears.\n\nIf you step forward and discover weakness, cry out to Him.\n\nFaith is not proving you can walk on water.\n\nIt is trusting the One who called you out of the boat.",
