    "reflection": "Luke tells us exactly why Jesus gave the parable of the persistent widow:\n\nHis disciples “ought always to pray, and not to faint.”\n\nSome prayers are answered quickly.\n\nOthers become companions for years.\n\nThe child you continue praying for.\n\nThe family situation that has not changed.\n\nThe direction you still need.\n\nThe person who does not yet know Christ.\n\nThe breakthrough that has not arrived.\n\nWaiting can make us wonder whether continued prayer matters.\n\nJesus tells us not to give up.\n\nBut persistence is not manipulation. We are not wearing down a reluctant God.\n\nJesus contrasts God with the unjust judge rather than comparing Him to one. If even an unjust judge eventually responds, how much more can God's people trust their righteous Father?\n\nKeep praying.\n\nAnd while you pray, allow God to work in you as well as in the situation.",
