    "reflection": "Waiting can feel like nothing is happening.\n\nBut Scripture repeatedly shows God working in waiting seasons.\n\nIsaiah says those who wait for the Lord will renew their strength.\n\nWaiting on God is not necessarily inactivity.\n\nYou may still work.\n\nPrepare.\n\nLearn.\n\nServe.\n\nApply.\n\nPray.\n\nDevelop.\n\nBut you refuse to force what God has not opened.\n\nWaiting exposes our desire for control.\n\nIt asks whether we trust God's wisdom when His timetable differs from ours.\n\nPerhaps you expected to be further ahead by now.\n\nPerhaps you thought the relationship, opportunity, ministry, family situation or answer would have arrived already.\n\nDon't assume delay means abandonment.\n\nUse the waiting room well.\n\nLet God deepen roots that future responsibility may require.",
