    "book": "deuteronomy",
    "chapter": 8,
    "reflection": "Israel's wilderness journey was uncomfortable, but it was also formative.\n\nMoses told the people to remember how God had led them through the wilderness, humbling and testing them and teaching them dependence.\n\nWilderness seasons expose what prosperity can hide.\n\nWhat do I depend upon?\n\nWhat controls me?\n\nWill I trust God when familiar comforts disappear?\n\nNot every hardship is a divine test we can neatly interpret. We should be careful about claiming to know precisely why suffering occurs.\n\nBut every difficult season can become a place where we learn deeper dependence upon God.\n\nThe wilderness may reveal impatience.\n\nFear.\n\nEntitlement.\n\nSelf-sufficiency.\n\nIt can also reveal God's provision.\n\nIf you are in a barren season, don't waste all your energy wishing you were somewhere else.\n\nAsk:\n\n“God, how can I walk faithfully with You here?”",
