    "reflection": "David begins Psalm 13 with a painful question:\n\n“How long, Yahweh? Will you forget me forever?”\n\nScripture makes room for prayers like this.\n\nFaith does not require pretending God always feels near.\n\nThere may be seasons when prayer feels unanswered and Scripture feels dry.\n\nThe psalm shows us what to do with that experience:\n\nbring it to God.\n\nDavid moves from lament to petition and finally to trust.\n\nHe does not deny his pain.\n\nHe processes it in God's presence.\n\nWhen God seems silent, resist the temptation to conclude automatically that He is absent.\n\nContinue praying.\n\nContinue reading His Word.\n\nContinue gathering with His people.\n\nContinue doing what you know is faithful.\n\nFeelings of distance are real.\n\nThey are not always reliable descriptions of God's actual presence.",
