    "slug": "grace-for-weakness",
    "title": "Grace for Weakness",
    "theme": "God's strength in weakness",
    "movement": "Walking by Faith",
    "scriptureReference": "2 Corinthians 12:9–10",
    "book": "2-corinthians",
    "chapter": 12,
    "reflection": "We live in a culture that celebrates strength.\n\nCompetence.\n\nIndependence.\n\nCapacity.\n\nWeakness feels embarrassing.\n\nYet Paul learned that weakness could become the place where Christ's power rested upon him.\n\nThis does not mean weakness itself is always good.\n\nNor should we refuse help, treatment, rest or practical solutions because we think struggling is somehow more spiritual.\n\nPaul's point is dependence.\n\nYour limitations remind you that you are not God.\n\nYou cannot do everything.\n\nYou cannot carry everyone.\n\nYou cannot meet every need.\n\nAnd you do not have to.\n\nGrace meets you where your own strength ends.\n\nSometimes the most faithful sentence you can say is:\n\n“I cannot do this without God.”\n\nThat is not failure.\n\nThat is dependence.",
