    "reflection": "“Let us not be weary in doing good.”\n\nWhy would Paul need to say this?\n\nBecause doing good can become tiring.\n\nYou serve and see little result.\n\nYou invest in people who do not respond.\n\nYou work faithfully without recognition.\n\nYou sow for years before seeing fruit.\n\nWeariness can tempt us to abandon good work simply because the harvest has not arrived.\n\nPaul tells us to continue.\n\nBut perseverance does not mean ignoring legitimate exhaustion.\n\nJesus rested.\n\nHuman beings need sleep, boundaries and rhythms of restoration.\n\nSometimes the faithful response to weariness is rest.\n\nThen continue.\n\nDon't confuse resting from the work with abandoning the work.",
