    "reflection": "Paul describes a progression:\n\nsuffering → perseverance → proven character → hope.\n\nMost of us would prefer to skip directly to hope.\n\nBut character is often forged through processes we would not voluntarily choose.\n\nPatience develops because something makes us wait.\n\nCourage develops because something makes us afraid.\n\nEndurance develops because something becomes difficult.\n\nForgiveness develops because somebody gives us something to forgive.\n\nWe should never seek unnecessary suffering.\n\nBut when difficulty comes, we can ask God to make us better rather than bitter.\n\nAnd Paul says hope does not disappoint because God's love has been poured into our hearts through the Holy Spirit.\n\nOur hope remains anchored in God even while character is being formed.",
