    "book": "2-timothy",
    "chapter": 4,
    "reflection": "Near the end of his life, Paul could say:\n\n“I have fought the good fight. I have finished the course. I have kept the faith.”\n\nThat is a powerful definition of success.\n\nNot:\n\nEveryone knew my name.\n\nNot:\n\nEverything I attempted became large.\n\nNot:\n\nLife unfolded exactly according to plan.\n\nBut:\n\nI kept the faith.\n\nChristian faithfulness is measured across a lifetime.\n\nThere will be seasons of extraordinary fruit and seasons of hidden obedience.\n\nSeasons of strength and seasons when continuing itself feels costly.\n\nThe goal is not simply to begin enthusiastically.\n\nIt is to finish faithfully.\n\nOne day, all the temporary measures of success will disappear.\n\nWhat will matter is whether we belonged to Christ and faithfully ran the race He gave us.\n\nSo don't spend your life trying to win someone else's race.\n\nRun yours.\n\nAnd keep the faith.",
