    "reflection": "Paul points us to Jesus as the supreme example of humility.\n\nThough worthy of glory, Christ humbled Himself and became obedient even to death on a cross.\n\nHumility does not mean thinking you have no gifts.\n\nIt does not require allowing others to mistreat you.\n\nAnd it does not mean pretending you are less capable than you are.\n\nBiblical humility is freedom from making yourself the centre.\n\nIt allows you to celebrate someone else's success.\n\nReceive correction.\n\nSay, “I was wrong.”\n\nServe without recognition.\n\nLearn from people.\n\nGive credit.\n\nListen.\n\nPride constantly asks:\n\n“How does this make me look?”\n\nHumility increasingly asks:\n\n“What would honour Christ and serve others?”",
