    "reflection": "Paul describes believers as being transformed into the Lord's image “from glory to glory” by the Spirit.\n\nSanctification is a process.\n\nThis is important because growth can feel frustratingly slow.\n\nYou may recognise attitudes you thought you had overcome.\n\nOld temptations may reappear.\n\nYou may compare yourself with someone who seems further ahead.\n\nDon't confuse unfinished transformation with absent transformation.\n\nLook back.\n\nAre you quicker to repent than you once were?\n\nMore aware of pride?\n\nMore compassionate?\n\nMore hungry for Scripture?\n\nMore willing to forgive?\n\nMore sensitive to sin?\n\nGrowth is not always dramatic.\n\nSometimes holiness develops quietly.\n\nAnd transformation is not ultimately a self-improvement project.\n\nPaul says it comes from the Lord, the Spirit.\n\nWe participate actively.\n\nBut God is the One transforming us.",
