    "book": "1-corinthians",
    "chapter": 13,
    "reflection": "Paul gives us a sobering picture.\n\nYou can speak impressively.\n\nUnderstand mysteries.\n\nPossess remarkable faith.\n\nGive generously.\n\nMake extraordinary sacrifices.\n\nAnd still miss something essential.\n\nLove.\n\nSpiritual gifts without love become noise.\n\nKnowledge without love can become pride.\n\nSacrifice without love can become performance.\n\nThis means Christian maturity cannot be measured merely by how gifted someone appears.\n\nThe deeper question is:\n\nAre we becoming more loving?\n\nNot merely toward people who are easy to love.\n\nToward difficult people.\n\nToward those who cannot advance our ambitions.\n\nToward people who disagree with us.\n\nToward those who need patience.\n\nLove is not the decorative finishing touch on Christianity.\n\nJesus placed it near the centre of discipleship.",
