    "slug": "love-is-patient-and-kind",
    "title": "Love Is Patient and Kind",
    "theme": "What love looks like",
    "movement": "Fruitful Living",
    "scriptureReference": "1 Corinthians 13:4–7",
    "book": "1-corinthians",
    "chapter": 13,
    "reflection": "“Love is patient and is kind.”\n\nWe often describe love as an emotion.\n\nPaul describes it through behaviour.\n\nLove waits.\n\nLove acts kindly.\n\nLove refuses envy.\n\nLove does not boast.\n\nLove is not arrogant.\n\nLove does not insist upon having its own way.\n\nThis makes 1 Corinthians 13 much more challenging than a beautiful wedding reading.\n\nPut your own name into the passage.\n\nAm I patient?\n\nAm I kind?\n\nDo I keep records of wrongs?\n\nDo I insist upon getting my way?\n\nThe passage quickly becomes a mirror.\n\nAnd when the reflection exposes us, the answer is not despair.\n\nIt is transformation.\n\nThe Spirit is producing this kind of love in us.\n\nEvery relationship becomes a place where we can practise it.",
