    "reflection": "John points to Jesus:\n\n“By this we know love, because he laid down his life for us.”\n\nThen John moves love from theology into practice.\n\nDon't love merely in word.\n\nLove in action and truth.\n\nReal love eventually costs something.\n\nTime.\n\nConvenience.\n\nAttention.\n\nResources.\n\nPride.\n\nForgiveness.\n\nSometimes love means showing up when you would rather stay home.\n\nSometimes it means listening when you are tired.\n\nSometimes it means giving.\n\nSometimes it means speaking a difficult truth rather than preserving comfortable silence.\n\nSacrificial love does not mean allowing yourself to be endlessly exploited.\n\nJesus' love was both sacrificial and truthful.\n\nBiblical love seeks another person's genuine good.\n\nAsk today:\n\nWhere can my love become practical?",
