    "reflection": "Paul writes:\n\n“Rejoice in the Lord always! Again I will say, rejoice!”\n\nThose words were not written from a life untouched by difficulty.\n\nPaul knew imprisonment, opposition, loss and suffering.\n\nYet notice where he locates joy:\n\nin the Lord.\n\nHe does not say:\n\nRejoice because every circumstance is wonderful.\n\nHe says:\n\nRejoice in the Lord.\n\nChristian joy becomes possible because its deepest object remains unchanged.\n\nGod's character does not deteriorate.\n\nChrist's resurrection does not expire.\n\nGrace does not run out.\n\nOur inheritance does not disappear when today is difficult.\n\nSometimes rejoicing is spontaneous.\n\nSometimes it is deliberate remembrance.\n\nYou remind your soul what remains true.",
