    "reflection": "James tells believers to consider trials an occasion for joy because tested faith produces endurance.\n\nHe is not telling suffering people to enjoy pain.\n\nThe joy comes from knowing the trial is not spiritually meaningless.\n\nGod can produce endurance through what we would never have chosen.\n\nThere are lessons comfort cannot teach.\n\nPatience requires waiting.\n\nEndurance requires difficulty.\n\nCourage requires something frightening enough to require courage.\n\nThe goal is not to seek hardship.\n\nBut when hardship comes, faith can ask:\n\n“God, what can You form in me here?”\n\nJoy sees beyond the immediate moment.\n\nIt believes suffering does not have the authority to waste the life surrendered to God.",
