    "reflection": "Paul tells believers to bring everything to God through prayer, petition and thanksgiving.\n\nThen he promises that God's peace will guard hearts and minds in Christ.\n\nNotice that prayer is not denial.\n\nYou name the concern.\n\nBring the request.\n\nAnd join it with thanksgiving.\n\nAnxiety tries to keep rehearsing the future as though repetition will create control.\n\nPrayer takes those same concerns and deliberately places them before God.\n\nSometimes you may need to do this repeatedly.\n\nThat is not failed faith.\n\nIt is dependence.\n\nEach time the concern returns, return it to God.\n\nPrayer may not immediately change the circumstance.\n\nBut God can guard the heart while the situation remains unresolved.",
