    "reflection": "Jesus said:\n\n“Blessed are the peacemakers.”\n\nThere is a difference between being a peacemaker and merely being a peacekeeper.\n\nPeacekeeping can mean avoiding difficult conversations so nobody becomes uncomfortable.\n\nPeacemaking may require entering conflict wisely to pursue truth and reconciliation.\n\nBiblical peace is not pretending everything is fine.\n\nSometimes peace requires apology.\n\nSometimes confrontation.\n\nSometimes listening.\n\nSometimes mediation.\n\nSometimes boundaries.\n\nA peacemaker does not unnecessarily inflame conflict, but neither does she sacrifice truth to preserve appearances.\n\nAsk yourself:\n\nWhen conflict arises, do I intensify it?\n\nAvoid it completely?\n\nOr seek to respond with truth, humility and grace?",
