    "reflection": "Paul tells believers to work sincerely rather than merely performing when people are watching.\n\nThat principle reaches far beyond employment.\n\nIntegrity is who you are when the audience disappears.\n\nWhen nobody will know whether you exaggerated.\n\nWhether you cut the corner.\n\nWhether you kept your word.\n\nWhether you viewed the content.\n\nWhether you returned the money.\n\nWhether you prayed.\n\nWhether you were faithful.\n\nCharacter is built in hidden decisions.\n\nWe can become so concerned with reputation—what people think we are—that we neglect character—what God knows we are.\n\nThe goal is not perfection.\n\nIt is increasing agreement between our private and public lives.\n\nLive before God.",
