    "book": "galatians",
    "chapter": 5,
    "reflection": "The Fruit of the Spirit ends with self-control.\n\nThat placement is significant.\n\nThe Spirit's work does not make us less responsible for our choices.\n\nIt increasingly enables us to govern desires rather than being governed by them.\n\nSelf-control says:\n\nI can feel angry without saying everything anger wants to say.\n\nI can desire something without automatically taking it.\n\nI can feel an impulse without obeying it.\n\nI can want another portion and still stop.\n\nI can want to send the message and decide to wait.\n\nI can want to purchase something and choose not to.\n\nFreedom is not doing everything you feel like doing.\n\nSometimes freedom is discovering that an appetite no longer owns you.",
