    "title": "Discipline Your Appetites",
    "theme": "Mastering appetites",
    "movement": "Fruitful Living",
    "scriptureReference": "1 Corinthians 6:12",
    "book": "1-corinthians",
    "chapter": 6,
    "reflection": "Paul makes a powerful statement:\n\n“I will not be brought under the power of anything.”\n\nNot everything permissible is beneficial.\n\nThat principle reaches into many areas.\n\nFood.\n\nShopping.\n\nEntertainment.\n\nSocial media.\n\nWork.\n\nExercise.\n\nApproval.\n\nEven good things can become controlling things.\n\nOne useful question is:\n\n“Can I comfortably say no to this?”\n\nIf the answer is repeatedly no, pay attention.\n\nSelf-control does not require treating every pleasure as suspicious.\n\nGod gives good gifts to enjoy with gratitude.\n\nBut gifts make terrible masters.\n\nSometimes fasting from a legitimate pleasure reveals how much authority it has quietly gained.\n\nFreedom includes the ability to enjoy something without needing it to rule you.",
