    "reflection": "Scripture says:\n\n“Be angry, and don't sin.”\n\nThat is remarkably balanced.\n\nThe Bible does not command us never to experience anger.\n\nIt commands us not to allow anger to lead us into sin.\n\nEmotions are signals.\n\nThey can tell us something has hurt, frightened, disappointed or angered us.\n\nBut signals are not always instructions.\n\nFeeling something does not automatically mean acting upon it is wise.\n\nSpiritual maturity is neither emotional explosion nor emotional suppression.\n\nIt is learning to bring emotions before God.\n\nName them.\n\nExamine them.\n\nUnderstand what is beneath them.\n\nThen choose a response consistent with truth.\n\nYou can feel deeply and still respond wisely.",
