    "book": "colossians",
    "chapter": 3,
    "reflection": "It is possible to appear wonderfully spiritual in public while being extremely difficult to live with privately.\n\nThat is why relationships are such important places of spiritual formation.\n\nLove becomes real when somebody irritates you.\n\nPatience becomes real when someone is slow.\n\nGentleness becomes real during disagreement.\n\nSelf-control becomes real when you are angry.\n\nKindness becomes real when you are tired.\n\nFruit is tested in proximity.\n\nAsk the people closest to you—not necessarily verbally, but through honest self-examination:\n\nWho experiences the most Christlike version of me?\n\nIs it strangers?\n\nChurch members?\n\nColleagues?\n\nOr the people who share ordinary life with me?\n\nThe Spirit wants fruit to grow at home too.",
