    "reflection": "“Strength and dignity are her clothing.”\n\nWhat a beautiful description.\n\nStrength and dignity are not accessories she occasionally puts on for public appearances.\n\nThey clothe her.\n\nBiblical strength is not hardness.\n\nDignity is not pride.\n\nA strong woman can still be gentle.\n\nA dignified woman can still be humble.\n\nStrength enables her to face responsibility without collapsing under every pressure.\n\nDignity reminds her that she does not have to degrade herself for attention, affection or opportunity.\n\nSome women have been taught that godliness means becoming smaller, quieter and less capable.\n\nScripture gives us a richer picture.\n\nA godly woman can possess strength.\n\nCompetence.\n\nCourage.\n\nWisdom.\n\nPresence.\n\nThe question is whether that strength remains submitted to God and used faithfully.",
