    "reflection": "“If any of you lacks wisdom, let him ask of God.”\n\nWhat a practical promise.\n\nGod does not shame us for admitting:\n\n“I do not know what to do.”\n\nWisdom is especially necessary when the Bible does not give a direct command concerning a specific decision.\n\nTwo jobs.\n\nTwo schools.\n\nA business opportunity.\n\nA difficult relationship.\n\nA parenting decision.\n\nA ministry direction.\n\nAsk God.\n\nThen remain attentive to the ways wisdom often comes:\n\nScripture.\n\nPrayer.\n\nMature counsel.\n\nFacts.\n\nExperience.\n\nProvidence.\n\nTime.\n\nSometimes we ask God for wisdom but resist the answer because wisdom does not favour the option we already wanted.\n\nSo ask with an open heart.",
