    "movement": "A Woman After God’s Heart",
    "scriptureReference": "Ecclesiastes 3:7",
    "book": "ecclesiastes",
    "chapter": 3,
    "reflection": "There is:\n\n“a time to keep silence, and a time to speak.”\n\nWisdom requires both.\n\nSome women have been silenced in situations where they needed courage to speak.\n\nOthers have spoken into situations where silence would have been wiser.\n\nBiblical wisdom refuses a simplistic rule.\n\nThere is a time to advocate.\n\nA time to confront.\n\nA time to ask questions.\n\nA time to testify.\n\nA time to defend someone vulnerable.\n\nAnd there is also a time to stop arguing.\n\nA time not to share the information.\n\nA time not to respond to provocation.\n\nA time to listen.\n\nA time to wait until emotions settle.\n\nSilence can be fear.\n\nBut silence can also be strength.\n\nSpeech can be courage.\n\nBut speech can also be impulsiveness.\n\nAsk God for discernment.",
    "declaration": "I will not speak merely because I can, nor remain silent merely because I am afraid. I will seek God’s wisdom concerning when to speak and when to be still.",
