    "title": "A Trustworthy Woman",
    "theme": "Integrity and reliability",
    "movement": "A Woman After God’s Heart",
    "scriptureReference": "Proverbs 31:11–12",
    "book": "proverbs",
    "chapter": 31,
    "reflection": "“The heart of her husband trusts in her.”\n\nAlthough Proverbs 31 describes a married woman, trustworthiness is a virtue relevant to every life stage.\n\nCan people safely trust your word?\n\nYour discretion?\n\nYour handling of money?\n\nYour responsibilities?\n\nYour confidentiality?\n\nYour promises?\n\nIntegrity creates trust slowly.\n\nIt can be damaged quickly.\n\nBeing trustworthy does not mean becoming available for every responsibility others want to hand you.\n\nHealthy limits remain necessary.\n\nIt means what you accept, you handle faithfully.\n\nWhat you promise, you take seriously.\n\nWhat is shared confidentially, you protect appropriately.\n\nWhat belongs to someone else, you do not misuse.\n\nGodly influence requires trust.\n\nCharacter sustains what gifting may initially open.",
    "declaration": "I want to be a trustworthy woman. I will handle words, responsibilities, relationships and resources with integrity and faithfulness.",
    "prayer": "Father, make me trustworthy in both small and significant matters. Reveal careless habits that damage confidence and teach me to honour what others and You entrust to me. Amen."
