    "book": "proverbs",
    "chapter": 31,
    "reflection": "“She arms her waist with strength, and makes her arms strong.”\n\nThe Proverbs 31 woman is not passive.\n\nShe develops capacity.\n\nThere are seasons when God may call you to become stronger.\n\nSpiritually.\n\nEmotionally.\n\nIntellectually.\n\nProfessionally.\n\nPractically.\n\nSometimes we pray for God to enlarge our opportunities while ignoring the development necessary to carry them.\n\nStrength may require learning.\n\nTraining.\n\nHealing.\n\nPractising.\n\nBuilding better systems.\n\nDeveloping discipline.\n\nGetting help.\n\nRestoring health where possible.\n\nSeeking mentorship.\n\nGrowing in Scripture.\n\nCapacity is stewardship.\n\nYou do not need to become capable of everything.\n\nYou need appropriate strength for what God has entrusted to you.\n\nAnd remember: strength includes knowing when you need help.",
