    "reflection": "“She seeks wool and flax, and works eagerly with her hands.”\n\nThe Proverbs 31 woman is willing to work.\n\nHer diligence is not presented as frantic striving. It is purposeful stewardship.\n\nThere is dignity in good work.\n\nPaid work.\n\nUnpaid work.\n\nWork within the home.\n\nWork in business.\n\nWork in ministry.\n\nCreative work.\n\nCaregiving.\n\nLearning.\n\nBuilding.\n\nThe form changes across seasons, but the principle remains: what God places in our hands deserves faithful attention.\n\nDiligence does not mean never resting.\n\nNor does productivity determine your worth.\n\nYour value was settled before today's task list began.\n\nThat security frees you to work from grace rather than for identity.\n\nWhatever today's assignment is, do it faithfully.",
