    "reflection": "“Whatever you do, work heartily, as for the Lord.”\n\nSome work feels obviously spiritual.\n\nTeaching Scripture.\n\nServing at church.\n\nPraying with someone.\n\nOther work feels ordinary.\n\nSpreadsheets.\n\nCleaning.\n\nMeetings.\n\nCooking.\n\nAdministration.\n\nCaring for children.\n\nStudying.\n\nServing customers.\n\nYet Scripture refuses to divide life neatly into sacred and secular.\n\nWork done faithfully before God can become worship.\n\nThat does not mean every workplace is healthy or every job must become your calling.\n\nSometimes wisdom means leaving harmful employment.\n\nBut while a responsibility is genuinely yours, Christ changes the audience.\n\nYou ultimately work before Him.\n\nThat can bring dignity to ordinary tasks and integrity to unseen ones.",
