    "slug": "willing-to-go",
    "title": "Willing to Go",
    "theme": "Willingness and courage",
    "movement": "Women of the Bible",
    "scriptureReference": "Genesis 24:55–58",
    "book": "genesis",
    "chapter": 24,
    "reflection": "When Rebekah was asked whether she would go, she answered:\n\n“I will go.”\n\nHer answer involved stepping into an unknown future.\n\nThere are moments when faith requires willingness before certainty.\n\nYou may not know every detail of the new season.\n\nThe job.\n\nThe move.\n\nThe responsibility.\n\nThe ministry opportunity.\n\nThe conversation.\n\nOf course, not every unfamiliar opportunity comes from God. Wisdom and discernment remain necessary.\n\nBut there are times when excessive demand for certainty becomes disguised fear.\n\nAfter prayer, wise counsel and appropriate evaluation, there comes a point when a decision must be made.\n\nSometimes courage sounds remarkably simple:\n\n“I will go.”",
