    "book": "exodus",
    "chapter": 15,
    "reflection": "After Israel crossed the sea, Miriam took a tambourine and led women in worship:\n\n“Sing to Yahweh, for he has triumphed gloriously.”\n\nMiriam's voice helped the community remember what God had done.\n\nThere is power in using your voice to direct attention toward God.\n\nYour voice may be musical.\n\nTeaching.\n\nWriting.\n\nEncouragement.\n\nPrayer.\n\nTestimony.\n\nConversation.\n\nLeadership.\n\nThe form differs.\n\nThe question is what your voice magnifies.\n\nWe live in a world where voices can easily become tools for self-promotion.\n\nMiriam reminds us that influence can become worship.\n\nTell people what God has done.\n\nGive thanks publicly.\n\nEncourage remembrance.\n\nLet your voice help others recognise His faithfulness.",
