    "slug": "pour-out-your-heart-before-god",
    "title": "Pour Out Your Heart Before God",
    "theme": "Honest prayer",
    "movement": "Women of the Bible",
    "scriptureReference": "1 Samuel 1:10–18",
    "book": "1-samuel",
    "chapter": 1,
    "reflection": "Hannah prayed from deep anguish.\n\nHer lips moved while her voice could not be heard.\n\nEli initially misunderstood her.\n\nGod did not.\n\nHer prayer reminds us that there is no requirement to tidy our emotions before bringing them to God.\n\nYou can pray while grieving.\n\nWhile disappointed.\n\nWhile longing.\n\nWhile confused.\n\nHonest prayer is not faithlessness.\n\nHannah poured out her soul.\n\nBut her story should not be turned into a formula:\n\n“Pray like Hannah and God will always give the exact thing you request.”\n\nHer particular story ended with Samuel.\n\nFaithful women throughout Scripture have also prayed prayers whose earthly outcomes differed from what they hoped.\n\nThe invitation remains:\n\nPour out your heart.\n\nThen entrust it to God.",
