    "reflection": "Mary's response to God's work became worship:\n\n“My soul magnifies the Lord.”\n\nHer song is saturated with Scripture and with the character of God.\n\nShe praises His holiness.\n\nMercy.\n\nPower.\n\nFaithfulness.\n\nJustice.\n\nMary's worship reveals something important:\n\nWhen the Word of God fills the heart, it becomes language for worship.\n\nWhat fills your mind will eventually shape what comes out of your mouth.\n\nMary's circumstances were still complicated.\n\nYet she deliberately magnified God.\n\nTo magnify the Lord does not mean making God bigger.\n\nHe cannot become greater than He is.\n\nIt means bringing His greatness into clearer view.\n\nSometimes anxiety magnifies the problem.\n\nWorship magnifies God.",
