    "reflection": "Martha was serving.\n\nService itself was not the problem.\n\nThe text says she became distracted by much serving.\n\nMary sat at Jesus' feet and listened.\n\nJesus said she had chosen the better portion.\n\nThis passage is not an argument that contemplative personalities are more spiritual than practical women.\n\nMartha's service mattered.\n\nBut service had become distraction.\n\nIt is possible to become so busy doing things for Jesus that we stop being attentive to Jesus.\n\nMinistry can do this.\n\nFamily responsibility can do this.\n\nEven a devotional project can do this.\n\nProductivity cannot replace presence.\n\nBefore asking:\n\n“What must I accomplish today?”\n\nlearn also to ask:\n\n“Am I listening to Jesus?”",
