    "scriptureReference": "Acts 16:14–15; Acts 18:24–26; Romans 16:1–4; 2 Timothy 1:5",
    "book": "acts",
    "chapter": 16,
    "reflection": "The New Testament gives us a remarkable picture of women participating in the growth of the early church.\n\nLydia responded to the gospel and opened her home, which became important to the emerging Christian community in Philippi.\n\nPriscilla, alongside Aquila, helped Apollos understand the way of God more accurately.\n\nPhoebe is commended by Paul to the Roman believers as a servant of the church and a benefactor of many.\n\nLois and Eunice cultivated sincere faith across generations, profoundly shaping Timothy.\n\nDifferent women.\n\nDifferent assignments.\n\nBusiness.\n\nHospitality.\n\nTeaching.\n\nService.\n\nGenerosity.\n\nDiscipleship.\n\nFamily influence.\n\nThe Kingdom does not require every woman to have the same role.\n\nIt calls every believer to faithful stewardship.\n\nDo not waste time trying to become somebody else's kind of useful.\n\nAsk:\n\n“How has God equipped me to participate faithfully in His mission?”\n\nThen serve.",
    "declaration": "There is a place for my gifts in God's mission. I will not compare my assignment with another woman's; I will faithfully use what God has entrusted to me to strengthen His Kingdom.",
    "prayer": "Father, thank You for the women throughout Scripture who served Your purposes in different ways. Show me how my gifts, experience, resources and relationships can strengthen Your work. Make me faithful in my generation. Amen.\n\nMovement 8 complete ✅\n\nDays 213–243 — Women of the Bible are now complete.\n\nThe full master journey stands at 243 of 365 devotionals drafted.\n\nMovement 8 has deliberately given us more than inspirational biographies. It has covered identity, temptation, waiting, rejection, comparison, worship, redemption, leadership, grief, prayer, wisdom, provision, purpose, surrender, sisterhood, perseverance, evangelism, resurrection, presence, growth, service and generational discipleship through the lives of biblical women.\n\nNext — Movement 9: Jesus — Knowing Him More Deeply\n\nFor Days 244–273, we can return completely to Jesus: His character, names, compassion, authority, teachings, prayer life, miracles, relationships, servant leadership, holiness, obedience, suffering, cross, resurrection, ascension, intercession, lordship and promised return.\n\nThis is important structurally too: the 365-day journey should never allow the woman's growth, purpose, family or ministry to become the centre. Jesus remains the centre.",
