    "reflection": "“Love is patient and is kind.”\n\nBiblical love contains emotion, but it is larger than emotion.\n\nLove acts.\n\nIt waits.\n\nServes.\n\nTells truth.\n\nForgives.\n\nRefuses envy.\n\nRejects arrogance.\n\nDoes not delight in wrongdoing.\n\nFeelings fluctuate.\n\nCovenantal love needs character capable of surviving fluctuation.\n\nThis applies beyond marriage.\n\nFriendship.\n\nFamily.\n\nChurch.\n\nParenting.\n\nSisterhood.\n\nAnd notice: biblical love does not rejoice in unrighteousness.\n\nLove therefore does not require pretending harmful behaviour is acceptable.\n\nSometimes love says yes.\n\nSometimes love says no.\n\nSometimes love embraces.\n\nSometimes love establishes a boundary.\n\nThe governing question is:\n\n“What genuinely seeks the good of this person before God?”",
