    "reflection": "Christian culture can sometimes speak as though adulthood begins at marriage.\n\nScripture does not.\n\nJesus was single.\n\nPaul speaks positively about the opportunities singleness can provide for undivided devotion.\n\nSome women desire marriage deeply.\n\nThat desire is legitimate.\n\nSome remain single for a season.\n\nSome much longer.\n\nSome intentionally.\n\nSingleness should not be romanticised—there can be real loneliness and longing.\n\nBut neither should it be treated as incomplete humanity.\n\nYou do not need to postpone purpose until someone chooses you.\n\nServe God now.\n\nBuild friendships now.\n\nDevelop your gifts now.\n\nTravel if appropriate.\n\nCreate.\n\nLearn.\n\nLead.\n\nGive.\n\nLove people.\n\nBecome rooted in Christ.\n\nMarriage may change your season.\n\nIt does not begin your significance.",
