    "reflection": "Healthy relationships require truthful communication.\n\nSome people emphasise truth while neglecting love.\n\nOthers emphasise peace while avoiding necessary truth.\n\nScripture joins them:\n\n“Speaking truth in love.”\n\nThat means saying what is true without using truth as a weapon.\n\nIt means addressing problems before resentment quietly grows.\n\nIt means listening rather than preparing your defence while the other person speaks.\n\nIt means refusing manipulation.\n\nSarcasm.\n\nContempt.\n\nSilent punishment.\n\nGossip disguised as concern.\n\nCommunication is not merely exchanging words.\n\nIt is learning to understand and be understood.\n\nBefore a difficult conversation, ask:\n\nIs it true?\n\nIs it necessary?\n\nIs this the right time?\n\nCan I say it with dignity?\n\nAm I willing to listen too?",
