    "reflection": "“Forgive each other... even as Christ forgave you.”\n\nForgiveness is central to Christian relationships because forgiven people are called to become forgiving people.\n\nBut forgiveness is often misunderstood.\n\nForgiveness does not mean saying the wrong did not matter.\n\nIt does not require calling evil good.\n\nIt does not necessarily restore trust immediately.\n\nIt does not always require returning a relationship to its previous form.\n\nForgiveness releases personal vengeance into God's hands.\n\nIt says:\n\n“I will not make repayment my life's mission.”\n\nSometimes forgiveness happens quickly.\n\nSometimes deep wounds require repeated surrender as memories and emotions resurface.\n\nThe foundation remains Christ.\n\nWe forgive not because the offence was insignificant, but because we ourselves live by extraordinary mercy.",
