    "book": "1-timothy",
    "chapter": 5,
    "reflection": "Scripture takes family care seriously.\n\nAs parents age, relationships can change.\n\nThe person who once cared for you may increasingly need your support.\n\nThis can involve practical decisions.\n\nAppointments.\n\nFinances.\n\nHousing.\n\nCompanionship.\n\nAdvocacy.\n\nAnd sometimes enormous emotional and physical demands.\n\nHonouring ageing parents does not mean one daughter must carry everything alone.\n\nFamilies should share responsibility where possible.\n\nProfessional support may be necessary.\n\nCaregivers also have limits.\n\nBut Christian faith should shape how we treat people when age reduces their independence.\n\nDignity does not diminish with strength.",
