    "reflection": "The Proverbs 31 woman recognises that her trading is profitable.\n\nScripture does not present profitable enterprise as inherently unspiritual.\n\nThe question is what governs it.\n\nWisdom.\n\nIntegrity.\n\nStewardship.\n\nGenerosity.\n\nThe fear of the Lord.\n\nProfit can provide stability.\n\nEmployment.\n\nInvestment.\n\nGenerosity.\n\nExpansion.\n\nSupport for ministry and family.\n\nBut profit becomes dangerous when it becomes ultimate.\n\nJesus asks what it benefits a person to gain the whole world and lose her soul.\n\nBuild.\n\nCreate.\n\nTrade.\n\nGrow.\n\nBut remain owned by Christ, not by the thing you are building.",
