    "declaration": "I do not have to do everything. I will seek clarity about the work God has genuinely entrusted to me and give myself faithfully to completing it.",
    "prayer": "Father, clarify my assignments. Give me courage to begin what You ask, perseverance to continue and wisdom to release what is no longer mine. May my work glorify You. Amen.\n\nMovement 11 complete ✅\n\nWe now have 323 of 365 master devotionals drafted.\n\nThis movement covers the remaining practical themes we needed: purpose, spiritual gifts, vocation, work, business, leadership, mentoring, stewardship, contentment and giving—without equating purpose with platform or generosity with a prosperity formula.\n\nNext is Movement 12 — The Gospel: Justified, Sanctified & Glorified, Days 324–343. That section will deliberately slow down and teach the theological foundations you asked for: sin, grace, repentance, salvation, justification, righteousness in Christ, adoption, union with Christ, sanctification, assurance, perseverance and glorification."
