    "reflection": "“What does it profit a man to gain the whole world, and forfeit his life?”\n\nJesus asks a question every ambitious person should revisit.\n\nWhat if you achieve the goal and lose what mattered most?\n\nYou can build something successful while your soul becomes increasingly empty.\n\nGain influence while losing integrity.\n\nIncrease income while neglecting family.\n\nBuild ministry while losing intimacy with God.\n\nReceive applause while becoming someone you no longer recognise.\n\nAchievement is a poor substitute for discipleship.\n\nThere is nothing wrong with building something excellent.\n\nBut success must remain submitted to Christ.\n\nAsk periodically:\n\nWhat is this pursuit producing in me?\n\nNot merely:\n\nWhat is it producing for me?",
