    "reflection": "God repeatedly told Joshua:\n\n“Be strong and courageous.”\n\nLeadership requires courage because responsibility means making decisions when outcomes are not guaranteed.\n\nBut God did not tell Joshua merely to become brave.\n\nHis courage was anchored in two realities:\n\nGod's presence.\n\nAnd:\n\nGod's Word.\n\nBiblical courage is not recklessness.\n\nIt is not refusing advice.\n\nIt is not pretending uncertainty does not exist.\n\nIt is the willingness to obey after prayer, wisdom and discernment have made the direction clear.\n\nSome decisions will disappoint people.\n\nSome assignments will stretch you.\n\nLeadership cannot be governed entirely by fear of criticism.\n\nStay close to God's Word.\n\nSeek wise counsel.\n\nThen have courage to move.",
