    "movement": "Hope, Perseverance & Eternity",
    "scriptureReference": "John 16:33",
    "book": "john",
    "chapter": 16,
    "reflection": "Jesus said:\n\n“In the world you have trouble; but cheer up! I have overcome the world.”\n\nChristianity does not promise a trouble-free life.\n\nJesus is remarkably honest.\n\nThere will be difficulty.\n\nDisappointment.\n\nOpposition.\n\nLoss.\n\nUncertainty.\n\nThe presence of trouble is therefore not automatic evidence that you are outside God’s will.\n\nJesus gives us something greater than the promise of permanent comfort:\n\nHe has overcome the world.\n\nYour peace is not rooted in the absence of trouble but in the victory and presence of Christ.\n\nSome trouble requires action.\n\nSome requires endurance.\n\nSome requires leaving a harmful situation.\n\nSome requires waiting.\n\nBut none requires believing that trouble is ultimately Lord.\n\nJesus is.",
