    "reflection": "“When you walk through the fire, you will not be burned.”\n\nNotice Scripture says when, not if.\n\nGod’s promise is not that His people never encounter waters or fire.\n\nIt is:\n\n“I will be with you.”\n\nWe naturally want God to keep every difficult circumstance away.\n\nSometimes He does.\n\nOther times His faithfulness is displayed by carrying us through what we would never have chosen.\n\nThe fire may change you.\n\nIt may expose what matters.\n\nStrip away false security.\n\nDeepen compassion.\n\nTeach dependence.\n\nBut do not assume every painful event has a simple explanation.\n\nWhat you can know is this:\n\nGod does not abandon His people inside difficulty.",
